All 15 tests pass. Here's a summary of the 10 bugs fixed across 3 files:

**`src/auth.py`** (2 bugs)
- `has_permission`: case-insensitive comparison — `required.lower() in [r.lower() for r in user_roles]`
- `is_admin_or_owner`: `and` → `or` (the docstring says "admin **OR** matches the resource owner")

**`src/inventory.py`** (4 bugs)
- `__init__`: mutable default `{}` shared across instances → `None` with `dict(initial)` copy
- `add`: overwrote stock (`self._stock[sku] = qty`) → accumulates (`self._stock.get(sku, 0) + qty`)
- `reserve`: used `>=` so reserving exactly the available qty raised `OutOfStock` → changed to `>`
- `release`: no guard against releasing more than reserved → added `ValueError` check

**`src/text_utils.py`** (3 bugs, 4 edits)
- `slugify`: didn't lowercase alnum chars → `char.lower()`
- `slugify`: `replace("--", "-")` only collapsed pairs, not longer runs → `re.sub(r"-+", "-", ...)`
- `truncate`: didn't account for suffix length in the slice → `text[:max_len - len(suffix)] + suffix`
